From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chrisohearn <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:33:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/93] ASoC: apple: macaudio: Add K114 with the speakers off

The K114s (14-inch M5 Pro MacBook Pro with the PROLED panel) has the sound
hardware of the K116s and the J714s according to its Apple device tree,
which matches the K116s's node for node: six SN012776 amps on the AOP's
"spkr" stream and a CS42L84 jack codec on "cout", in the same frames. The
K116 entry reuses macaudio_j714_cfg, which admits the speakers under the
kernel's volume lock.

For K114 there is no speaker protection data: speakersafetyd has no k114
profile, speakerguardd v2 keeps K114 and K116 muted (its LSID unit is not
at parity), and nothing has been measured on this chassis. Give it its own
entry with J714's jack configuration and enable_speakers = false, as J873
and J604 have: macaudio_speakers_allowed() then refuses a "Speaker" link
whatever the device tree says, the speaker controls are not created, and
the jack works alone. The amp type and layout stay J714's and are not
used while enable_speakers is false; admitting the speakers needs
protection data for this chassis first.

The admission KUnit case asserts the refusal.

Not tested on the hardware. The K114c (M5 Max) shares the chassis name; its
device tree was not checked for this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>

[re-cut onto integration/aurora 0bbe021a for the K114s]
---
 .../bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml        |  1 +
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio-admission-test.h     |  2 ++
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c                    | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml
index c9880a39e9b..d1f19d065da 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,macaudio.yaml
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@ properties:
               - apple,j813-macaudio
               - apple,j815-macaudio
               - apple,j873-macaudio
+              - apple,k114-macaudio
               - apple,k116-macaudio
           - const: apple,macaudio
       - description:
diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio-admission-test.h b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio-admission-test.h
index 17c7f19c9cd..c5bf73b7556 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio-admission-test.h
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio-admission-test.h
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ static void macaudio_admission_needs_a_safe_level(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, macaudio_speakers_allowed(&macaudio_j873_cfg));
 	/* The Mac Studio M5: no sense and no protection owner yet, speaker off */
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, macaudio_speakers_allowed(&macaudio_j775_cfg));
+	/* K114: J714's layout, but no protection data for the chassis */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, macaudio_speakers_allowed(&macaudio_k114_cfg));
 	cfg = macaudio_j413_cfg;
 	cfg.safe_vol = 0;
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, macaudio_speakers_allowed(&cfg));
diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index ae4c96a816f..b38474b32d0 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -4191,6 +4191,30 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j714_cfg = {
 	.tweeter_hpf_granted = true,
 };
 
+/*
+ * K114 (T6050, MacBook Pro 14" M5 Pro with the PROLED panel; K114s):
+ * J714's AOP-fed card, with the CS42L84 jack on "cout" in the same frame.
+ * No speaker protection data exists for this chassis (no speakersafetyd
+ * profile, no qualified speakerguardd tuning), and nothing has been
+ * measured on it, so there is no safe level: macaudio_speakers_allowed()
+ * keeps the speakers off as on J873, whatever the device tree links. The
+ * jack is unaffected. The amp type and layout are the J714's and are not
+ * used while enable_speakers is false; admitting the speakers needs
+ * protection data for this chassis first.
+ */
+struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_k114_cfg = {
+	.enable_speakers = false,
+	.amp = AMP_SN012776,
+	.speakers = SPKR_2W1T,
+	.stereo = true,
+	.safe_vol = -20,
+	.fe_dai_names = { "j873-pcm-0", "j873-pcm-1", "j873-pcm-2" },
+	.dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_DSP_A | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_IB_NF,
+	.spk_dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC |
+		       SND_SOC_DAIFMT_GATED | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_IF,
+	.spk_secondary_only = true,
+};
+
 /*
  * J815 (T8142, MacBook Air M5 15"): J813's AOP-fed card with six SN012776,
  * two woofers and a tweeter per side, in ADT speaker-config order (left
@@ -4502,6 +4526,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id macaudio_snd_device_id[]  = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j714-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j714_cfg },
 	/* k116    -       sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed, V/I sense; the 16" PROLED chassis, J714's amps and frame) */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,k116-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j714_cfg },
+	/* k114    -       sn012776    -       the jack only: speakers off, no protection data (AOP-fed) */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,k114-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_k114_cfg },
 	/* j713    -       sn012776    15      2x 1W+1T (AOP-fed, one serializer) */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j713-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j713_cfg },
 	/* The J713 jack runs on the AOP like the J616s one. */
